- v2.2 -

    - Release Date: October 8, 1995!
    - Small update to bring this archive up to par for the 3.05c series:
        - New error checking routine in place.
        - Now uses a REAL version string.

- v2.1 -

    - It was brought to my attention that the "CNet21" font was lacking
      certain IBM graphics characters which gave the display of the screen
      an oddball effect to the SysOp.
    - Because a lot of SysOps still use the "CNet21" font (WHY?!?!?), I
      had to rewrite the graphic routines slightly to use a period and
      asterisk to display the stars, instead of the extended IBM graphics.
    - Release Date: June 30, 1993!

- v2.0 -

    - FIRST VERSION By Dotoran!
    - Quotes now saved in PACKED CHARACTER format for SuperFast Displaying.
    - GRAPHICS were added of the Enterprise, and a planet & surrounding
      fun objects(moons, stars, etc.)
    - The Planet stuff is COLOR CUSTOMIZABLE to give the illusion of seeing
      a new planet every quote.
    - Release Date: June 29, 1993.

- v1.? -

    - Somewhere in this area.
    - Seem to recall a fixed version where the quotes weren't being shown
      correctly. You'd get the last line of one quote, then the beginning
      of the next quote.

- v1.0 -

    - Original version by Dan of Liesure World BBS.
    - Used a modified form of Jim Selleck's Random Quote Generator.
    - Contained 130 Trek Quotes.

